.MCD 25000 0
.CMD SURFACEFORMAT rot=10 tilt=35 vScale=20 size=15,30
.CMD SKETCHFORMAT mag=1.000000,1.000000 center=0.500000,0.500000 size=15,30 box=y
.CMD PLOTFORMAT logs=0,0 subdivs=1,1 size=5,15 type=l
.CMD FORMAT  rd=d ct=10 im=i et=3 zt=15 pr=3 mass length time charge
.CMD SET ORIGIN 0
.CMD SET TOL 0.001000000000000
.CMD MARGIN 0
.CMD LINELENGTH 78
.CMD SET PRNCOLWIDTH 8
.CMD SET PRNPRECISION 4
.TXT 0 0 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,90
420spd.mcd to show the effects of phase distortion in the channel's  frequency 
response.
.TXT 3 0 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,82
1. Define the degraded phase of the channel's frequency response- in 'DFT 
form'.
.EQN 3 0 1 10 
N:128
.EQN 0 13 1 16 
n:0;N-1
.EQN 0 17 1 12 
j:0;2
.EQN 0 14 2 13 
î[j:0.1*j
.EQN 0 16 3 10 
ç:(2*ã)/8
.EQN 2 -60 2 23 
é[(n,j):2*î[j*sin(ç*n)
.EQN 2 14 2 61 
H[(n,j):if(nó8,exp(1i*é[(n,j)),if(nò120,exp(1i*é[(N-n,j)),0))
.EQN 3 -6 8 58 
ã&-ã&é[(n,0),é[(n,1),é[(n,2){1,1,7,35,l}@N-1&0&n
.TXT 9 -8 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,135
2. Define the pulse whose spectrum has been shaped for low sidelobes: We 
choose a simple model, the triangle spectrum- in 'DFT form'.
.EQN 3 0 2 45 
P[n:if(nó8,8-n,if(nò120,n-120,0))
.EQN 0 50 7 20 
&&P[n{1,1,6,15,l}@N-1&0&n
.TXT 8 -50 1 32003 
b1,32002,78,35
3. Compute the output pulse, s(t).
.EQN 2 0 4 25 
idft(v):(1/\N)*cfft(v)
.EQN 1 25 2 17 
S[(n,j):H[(n,j)*P[n
.EQN 0 22 2 20 
s{52}j:idft(S{52}j)
.EQN 4 -47 3 17 
M[j:max(s{52}j)
.EQN 0 20 5 14 
s[(n,j):s[(n,j)/M[j
.EQN 4 -3 9 64 
0&-40&20*log(|s{52}j[n+0.000001){4,8,8,35,l}@N-1&0&n
.EQN 2 -17 3 13 
î=?
.EQN 4 0 1 13 
ç=?
.TXT 4 0 2 32003 
b2,32002,78,99
Thus phase errors of 10% or so negate the extra bandwidth devoted to 
controlling sidelobe levels.
